    "q-80612": {
      "dom_id": "step-q80612",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)={e}^{t}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t),$ we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${T}^{′}(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =|-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}|\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\sqrt{({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)+({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\sqrt{1+1+0} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =1 \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)+({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)+(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{1+1+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{t}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{-t}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
